# Line endings, settled once.
#
# Without this file the repository's own checkout was rewriting it. Every
# working tree here came out with CRLF against LF blobs, so `git status` showed
# 70 files modified with zero changed content — noise that hides real work and
# trains you to `git add .` past it.
#
# Worse, `Dageraad-status.pdf` was being converted too: 252 CR bytes injected
# into a binary, shifting every byte offset its xref table points at. A PDF
# that git thinks is text is a PDF git will corrupt on checkout.

# Normalise text to LF in the repository and in the working tree. All of this
# project's tooling is node, which does not care, and one representation
# everywhere means the diff is always the change.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touch these. Marked explicitly rather than left to git's guess, because
# the guess is what damaged the PDF.
*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.jar   binary
*.gz    binary
*.zip   binary
*.bundle binary
